step by step...\n\nContinuing the hash computation through the remaining characters, then converting the final accumulated value to hexadecimal by successive division.\n\nGood, so the hex value works out to 0xDF286663, giving hash3 = \"HDLmClassdf286663\".\n\nNow trying improvement 4, I want something shorter than \"Added book covers list\" - testing \"Added intro text\" with \"Sets context fast\" as the reason, giving a 33-character string. I'll reuse the \"Added \" prefix computation from improvement 2 and continue running the hash calculation through the remaining characters.\n\nContinuing the hash computation through the remaining characters x, t, S, e, t...\n\nContinuing the modular hash computation through characters n, t, e, x, t, and space, tracking the running value at each step.\n\nFinishing the hex conversion gives 0xB8E35CDA, so hash4 becomes \"HDLmClassb8e35cda\". Now I'm drafting improvement 5, considering options like adding a free-read note or grouping books by year to raise engagement.\n\nSettling on What: \"Added top CTA button\", Why: \"Drives quick action\", concatenated string length 39. I'm now grinding through the multiplicative hash computation character by character, tracking each intermediate value through the modular arithmetic.\n\nContinuing the modular hash computation through the remaining characters \"ton D\" step by step.\n\nContinuing the modular hash computation through characters 27-32 (space, q, u, i, c, k), tracking each multiply-by-33 step and reducing mod 2^32 before adding the ASCII value.\n\nContinuing the multiplicative hash through o(111) and n(110), I get 57975814 as the final accumulator, then convert it to hex to get 0x374A406, giving me the hash string \"HDLmClass374\" so far.\n\nFor improvement 6, I'm computing a hash of the string combining \"Added mobile meta tag\" and \"Fits small screens\" (39 chars), reusing the prefix hash for \"Added \" and continuing the multiply-mod-2^32 loop through m, o, b, i.\n\ne., l, sp, 