ntinuing the modular hash computation through the remaining characters \"ton D\" step by step.\n\nContinuing the modular hash computation through characters 27-32 (space, q, u, i, c, k), tracking each multiply-by-33 step and reducing mod 2^32 before adding the ASCII value.\n\nContinuing the multiplicative hash through o(111) and n(110), I get 57975814 as the final accumulator, then convert it to hex to get 0x374A406, giving me the hash string \"HDLmClass374\" so far.\n\nFor improvement 6, I'm computing a hash of the string combining \"Added mobile meta tag\" and \"Fits small screens\" (39 chars), reusing the prefix hash for \"Added \" and continuing the multiply-mod-2^32 loop through m, o, b, i.\n\ne., l, sp, m, e for each character.\n\nStill computing the hash iterations...\n\nContinuing the hash computation through characters c, r, e, e, n, applying the multiply-and-mod-reduce steps for each.\n\nFinishing letters \"s\" and converting the final accumulator to hex, I get 0xD35714B4, giving hash6 = \"HDLmClassd35714b4\". With six improvements settled, I'm considering adding a seventh item, perhaps a footer or SEO meta description enhancement.\n\nNow I'm turning to writing the actual HTML: preserving the existing scripts, image, and links while fixing the search form to properly wrap the hidden inputs in a form pointing to Google's CSE endpoint so it's functional, and structuring the page with a hero section, intro text, a CTA button linking to the first chapter, and a styled card grid of book links with year badges.\n\nNow I'll assemble the final HTML as the escaped JSON output, keeping all links and text intact aside from the typo fix.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":""}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":3073,"completion_tokens":18356,"total_tokens":21429,"cost":0.474265,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.474265,"upstream_inf