original publication order. Click any title to open the full text.</p>\\n    <ul class=\\\"booklist\\\">\\n      <li><a href=\\\"01.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">1</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Wonderful Wizard of Oz</span><span class=\\\"flag\\\">Start here</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1900</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"extra\\\"><a href=\\\"OzPlay.pdf\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">PDF</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Wizard of Oz: A Dramatic Composition</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1902 &middot; stage play</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li><a href=\\\"02.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">2</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Marvelous Land of Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1904</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li><a href=\\\"03.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">3</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">Ozma of Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1907</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li><a href=\\\"04.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">4</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">Dorothy and the Wizard in Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1908</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li><a href=\\\"05.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">5</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Road to Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1909</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li><a href=\\\"06.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">6</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Emerald City of Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1910</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li><a href=\\\"07.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">7</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Patchwork Girl of Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1913</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"extra\\\"><a href=\\\"08.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">+</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">Little Wizard Stories of Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1913 &middot; short stories</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li><a href=\\\"09.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">8</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">Tik-Tok of Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1914</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li><a href=\\\"10.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">9</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Scarecrow of Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1915</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li><a href=\\\"11.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">10</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">Rinkitink in Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1916</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li><a href=\\\"12.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">11</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Lost Princess of Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1917</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li><a href=\\\"13.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">12</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Tin Woodman of Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1918</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li><a href=\\\"14.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">13</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Magic of Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1919</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li><a href=\\\"15.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">14</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">Glinda of Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1920</span></span></a></li>\\n    </ul>\\n  </div>\\n</section>\\n\\n<section class=\\\"HDLmClass9a17d3be\\\">\\n  <div class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n    <div class=\\\"searchbox\\\">\\n      <h2>Search inside the Oz books</h2>\\n      <p class=\\\"section-sub\\\">Looking for a character, place or favorite scene? Search the full collection.</p>\\n      <form action=\\\"https://www.google.com/cse\\\" method=\\\"get\\\" id=\\\"cse-search-box\\\">\\n        <input type=\\\"hidden\\\" name=\\\"cx\\\" value=\\\"002807121847390519013:ddj9f84mdsw\\\" />\\n        <input type=\\\"hidden\\\" name=\\\"ie\\\" value=\\\"UTF-8\\\" />\\n        <label for=\\\"ozq\\\" style=\\\"position:absolute;left:-9999px;\\\">Search the Oz books</label>\\n        <input type=\\\"text\\\" id=\\\"ozq\\\" name=\\\"q\\\" size=\\\"31\\\" placeholder=\\\"Try &quot;Emerald City&quot; or &quot;Tin Woodman&quot;\\\" />\\n        <input type=\\\"submit\\\" name=\\\"sa\\\" value=\\\"Search the books\\\" />\\n      </form>\\n    </div>\\n  </div>\\n</section>\\n\\n<section class=\\\"HDLmClass6d52b8c9\\\" style=\\\"padding-top:0;\\\">\\n  <div class=\\\"wrap\\\" style=\\\"text-align:center;\\\">\\n    <h2>New to Oz? Begin at the beginning.</h2>\\n    <p class=\\\"section-sub\\\">Dorothy's first journey down the yellow brick road is still the best place to start.</p>\\n    <a class=\\\"btn btn-primary\\\" href=\\\"01.htm\\\">Read The Wonderful Wizard of Oz &rarr;</a>\\n  </div>\\n</section>\\n\\n<footer class=\\\"HDLmClass6d52b8c9\\\">\\n  <div class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n    All 14 Oz novels by L. Frank Baum (1856&ndash;1919) are in the public domain and free to read here. <a href=\\\"#books\\\">Back to the book list</a>.\\n  </div>\\n</footer>\\n\\n<script type=\\\"text/javascript\\\" src=\\\"https://www.google.com/coop/cse/brand?form=cse-search-box&lang=en\\\"></script>\\n</body>\\n</html>\",\"improvements\":[{\"What\":\"Added a mobile viewport meta tag, character set, lang attribute and a keyword-rich meta description plus an improved SEO page title.\",\"Why\":\"The original page had no viewport or description, so it rendered tiny on phones and had weak search snippets. Mobile-legible pages and descriptive snippets bring more qualified visitors and reduce bounce.\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass3f7a91c4\"},{\"What\":\"Built a hero section with a clear value proposition headline, supporting sub-copy, the existing Lion illustration (now with descriptive alt text) and two prominent calls to action ('Start reading Book 1' and 'Browse all books').\",\"Why\":\"Visitors previously landed on an unexplained image and a bare list of links. A hero that states what the site offers and gives one obvious next step dramatically increases click-through into the content.\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass8b21e6a7\"},{\"What\":\"Added a trust/benefit bar highlighting 'free', 'no signup', 'read instantly' and 'complete unabridged texts'.\",\"Why\":\"Removing perceived cost and friction up front reassures first-time visitors and raises the rate at which they start reading instead of leaving to find another source.\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass5c9d4a12\"},{\"What\":\"Converted the plain link list into a responsive, scannable card grid with numbered badges, bolded titles, publication years, a 'Start here' flag on Book 1, and large tap-friendly hover targets; also corrected the typo 'The Wonderful Wixard of Oz' to 'Wizard'.\",\"Why\":\"Bigger, clearly separated, easy-to-tap targets improve usability on mobile and make choosing a book effortless, while the typo fix protects credibility and search relevance.\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass2e84c7f3\"},{\"What\":\"Made the search box a working, labeled Google CSE form with a real form action, heading, explanatory copy, placeholder examples and a descriptive 'Search the books' button.\",\"Why\":\"The original inputs were not inside a form, so searches could not be submitted at all; a functional, clearly explained search helps visitors find what they want and keeps them on the site.\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass9a17d3be\"},{\"What\":\"Added a closing call-to-action block recommending Book 1 plus a simple footer with public-domain context and a link back to the book list.\",\"Why\":\"A repeated CTA at the end of the page captures readers who scrolled without choosing, and the public-domain note builds trust and legitimacy.\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass6d52b8c9\"}]}","refusal":null,"reasoning":"I'm improving the HTML by fixing the \"Wixard\" typo to \"Wonderful Wizard,\" adding a hero section, descriptions, a working search form tied to Google CSE, responsive styling, alt text, and proper meta tags. I also need to compute DJB2 hashes by hand for each string, iterating hash = hash*33 + charCode mod 2^32 and converting to hex.\n\nNow I'm writing out the full HTML with these changes, planning improvements like a hero headline, trust/benefit bar, book cover CTA, footer links, and lazy-loaded images while keeping the original scripts intact.","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm improving the HTML by fixing the \"Wixard\" typo to \"Wonderful Wizard,\" adding a hero section, descriptions, a working search form tied to Google CSE, responsive styling, alt text, and proper meta tags. I also need to compute DJB2 hashes by hand for each string, iterating hash = hash*33 + charCode mod 2^32 and converting to hex.\n\nNow I'm writing out the full HTML with these changes, planning improvements like a hero headline, trust/benefit bar, book cover CTA, footer links, and lazy-loaded images while keeping the original scripts intact.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":""}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":3047,"completion_tokens":7303,"total_tokens":10350,"cost":0.19781,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.19781,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.015235,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.182575},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":646,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}
