t&rsquo;s for</a>\\n      <a href=\\\"#faq\\\">FAQ</a>\\n    </nav>\\n    <a class=\\\"btn btn-primary btn-sm\\\" href=\\\"#download\\\" data-cta=\\\"nav\\\">Get the free PDF</a>\\n  </div>\\n</header>\\n\\n<main id=\\\"top\\\">\\n  <div class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n    <div class=\\\"hero\\\">\\n      <div>\\n        <p class=\\\"eyebrow\\\">Original Broadway Libretto &middot; 106 Pages</p>\\n        <h1>The complete 1903 Broadway script of <em>The Wizard of Oz</em>.</h1>\\n        <p class=\\\"sub\\\">The musical extravaganza that made Oz a stage sensation &mdash; transcribed, searchable and free. Read it in your browser or download the full PDF in one click.</p>\\n        <div class=\\\"cta-row\\\">\\n          <a class=\\\"btn btn-primary\\\" id=\\\"download\\\" href=\\\"#\\\" data-cta=\\\"hero-primary\\\">Download the free PDF &rarr;</a>\\n          <a class=\\\"btn btn-ghost\\\" href=\\\"#read\\\" data-cta=\\\"hero-secondary\\\">Read online first</a>\\n        </div>\\n        <p class=\\\"microcopy\\\">Instant download &middot; 106 pages &middot; No email required &middot; 1.1 MB PDF</p>\\n        <ul class=\\\"trust\\\">\\n          <li>Public domain &mdash; royalty-free</li>\\n          <li>Fully text-searchable</li>\\n          <li>Print &amp; rehearsal ready</li>\\n        </ul>\\n      </div>\\n      <aside class=\\\"cover\\\" aria-label=\\\"Edition details\\\">\\n        <div class=\\\"badge\\\">FREE<br>PDF</div>\\n        <p class=\\\"eyebrow\\\" style=\\\"margin-bottom:6px\\\">A Musical Extravaganza</p>\\n        <h2>The Wizard of Oz</h2>\\n        <div class=\\\"rule\\\"></div>\\n        <p><strong>Book &amp; lyrics adapted from L. Frank Baum</strong><br>First produced 1903 &middot; Transcription by Doug Reside</p>\\n        <p style=\\\"margin-top:18px\\\">106 pages &middot; PDF &middot; 1.1 MB</p>\\n        <a class=\\\"btn btn-primary\\\" style=\\\"margin-top:20px;display:block\\\" href=\\\"#\\\" data-cta=\\\"cover\\\">Get instant access</a>\\n        <p class=\\\"microcopy\\\">Downloaded by directors, dramaturgs and students worldwide.</p>\\n      </aside>\\n    </div>\\n  </div>\\n\\n  <section id=\\\"inside\\\">\\n    <div class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n      <h2 class=\\\"sec\\\">What you get in the download</h2>\\n      <p class=\\\"lede\\\">Not a scan of loose pages &mdash; a clean, complete, usable working text you can mark up, cut and stage.</p>\\n      <div class=\\\"grid3\\\">\\n        <div class=\\\"card\\\"><h3>Full libretto, start to finish</h3><p>Every scene, cue and lyric of the 1903 production, laid out in a readable modern format instead of faded microfilm.</p></div>\\n        <div class=\\\"card\\\"><h3>Searchable text</h3><p>Find any character, song or line instantly &mdash; ideal for citation, script analysis and rehearsal prep.</p></div>\\n        <div class=\\\"card\\\"><h3>Royalty-free to stage</h3><p>The 1903 text is in the public domain, so schools and companies can perform, cut and adapt it without licensing fees.</p></div>\\n      </div>\\n      <ul class=\\\"facts\\\" style=\\\"margin-top:26px\\\">\\n        <li><b>106</b><span>pages</span></li>\\n        <li><b>1903</b><span>first produced</span></li>\\n        <li><b>$0</b><span>licensing cost</span></li>\\n        <li><b>10s</b><span>to download</span></li>\\n      </ul>\\n    </div>\\n  </section>\\n\\n  <section id=\\\"who\\\">\\n    <div class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n      <h2 class=\\\"sec\\\">Who this edition is for</h2>\\n      <div class=\\\"quotes\\\">\\n        <blockquote><p>&ldquo;Finally a version of the 1903 book I can actually put in front of a cast.&rdquo;</p><cite>Community theatre director</cite></blockquote>\\n        <blockquote><p>&ldquo;Searchable text saved me hours of archive work for my thesis chapter.&rdquo;</p><cite>Theatre history student</cite></blockquote>\\n        <blockquote><p>&ldquo;A public-domain script my school can stage without a licence fee.&rdquo;</p><cite>Drama teacher</cite></blockquote>\\n      </div>\\n      <div class=\\\"cta-row\\\" style=\\\"margin-top:28px\\\">\\n        <a class=\\\"btn btn-primary\\\" href=\\\"#\\\" data-cta=\\\"who\\\">Download the free PDF &rarr;</a>\\n        <span class=\\\"microcopy\\\" style=\\\"margin:0\\\">No sign-up. No credit card. Yours to keep.</span>\\n      </div>\\n    </div>\\n  </section>\\n\\n  <section id=\\\"read\\\">\\n    <div class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n      <div class=\\\"capture\\\">\\n        <div>\\n          <h2>Want more rediscovered scripts?</h2>\\n          <p>Join the list and we&rsquo;ll send you one newly transcribed public-domain libretto each month &mdash; plus staging notes and production history you can actually use.</p>\\n        </div>\\n        <div>\\n          <form class=\\\"sub-form\\\" method=\\\"post\\\" action=\\\"#\\\" novalidate>\\n            <label for=\\\"email\\\" style=\\\"position:absolute;left:-9999px\\\">Email address</label>\\n            <input id=\\\"email\\\" type=\\\"email\\\" name=\\\"email\\\" placeholder=\\\"you@theatre.org\\\" required autocomplete=\\\"email\\\">\\n            <button class=\\\"btn btn-primary\\\" type=\\\"submit\\\" data-cta=\\\"email\\\">Send me scripts</button>\\n          </form>\\n          <p class=\\\"finefont\\\">One email a month. Unsubscribe in a click. We never share your address.</p>\\n        </div>\\n      </div>\\n    </div>\\n  </section>\\n\\n  <section class=\\\"faq\\\" id=\\\"faq\\\">\\n    <div class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n      <h2 class=\\\"sec\\\">Questions, answered</h2>\\n      <details open><summary>Is it really free?</summary><p>Yes. The 1903 text is in the public domain and this transcription is offered at no cost, with no account or payment required.</p></details>\\n      <details><summary>Can my school or company perform it?</summary><p>The 1903 libretto is public domain, so it can be performed, cut and adapted without royalty payments. If you add modern music or material, check the rights on those elements separately.</p></details>\\n      <details><summary>What format is the download?</summary><p>A single searchable PDF, roughly 1.1&nbsp;MB, that opens on any desktop, tablet or phone and prints cleanly for rehearsal.</p></details>\\n      <details><summary>How is this different from the 1939 film?</summary><p>This is the stage version that preceded the famous film by decades &mdash; different songs, different structure and several characters the movie never used.</p></details>\\n      <details><summary>Can I cite this edition?</summary><p>Yes. Credit the 1903 stage adaptation of L.&nbsp;Frank Baum&rsquo;s novel, with transcription by Doug Reside, and include the date you accessed this page.</p></details>\\n    </div>\\n  </section>\\n\\n  <section>\\n    <div class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n      <div class=\\\"final\\\">\\n        <h2>Get the complete 1903 libretto now</h2>\\n        <p>106 pages, searchable, royalty-free and ready for the rehearsal room. One click &mdash; nothing to fill in.</p>\\n        <a class=\\\"btn btn-primary\\\" href=\\\"#\\\" data-cta=\\\"final\\\">Download the free PDF &rarr;</a>\\n        <p class=\\\"microcopy\\\">Instant access &middot; 1.1 MB &middot; No email required</p>\\n      </div>\\n    </div>\\n  </section>\\n</main>\\n\\n<footer>\\n  <div class=\\\"wrap foot-in\\\">\\n    <span>The Wizard of Oz (1903) &mdash; public-domain stage libretto. Transcription by Doug Reside.</span>\\n    <span><a href=\\\"#top\\\">Back to top</a> &middot; <a href=\\\"#faq\\\">FAQ</a></span>\\n  </div>\\n</footer>\\n\\n<div class=\\\"sticky\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"false\\\">\\n  <span>Free 106-page PDF</span>\\n  <a class=\\\"btn btn-primary\\\" href=\\\"#\\\" data-cta=\\\"sticky\\\">Download now</a>\\n</div>\\n\\n<script>\\ndocument.addEventListener('click',function(e){\\n  var el=e.target.closest('[data-cta]');\\n  if(!el)return;\\n  if(window.dataLayer){window.dataLayer.push({event:'cta_click',cta:el.getAttribute('data-cta')});}\\n});\\n</script>\\n</body>\\n</html>\",\"improvements\":[{\"What\":