ant delivery and no expiration communicates the actual value props of an e-gift card and supports last-minute gift purchases.\", \"Hash\": \"d914b6a3\"}, {\"What\": \"Changed the CTA button text from 'Add To Cart' to 'Buy Gift Card' on all three products.\", \"Why\": \"Action-specific CTA copy matched to the product type increases click-through; 'Buy Gift Card' reinforces the simple, one-step nature of the purchase and converts better than generic cart language for gifting flows.\", \"Hash\": \"e2c74f88\"}, {\"What\": \"Added a gift card FAQ section below the product grid (delivery, expiration, redemption) with a phone support prompt, plus matching FAQPage JSON-LD structured data in the head.\", \"Why\": \"Answering common pre-purchase questions on-page reduces abandonment and support inquiries, while FAQ schema can earn rich results in Google, increasing SERP real estate and traffic.\", \"Hash\": \"f6091bd7\"}, {\"What\": \"Fixed the broken nested anchor tag in the mobile menu contact block ('Call Us / Mail us').\", \"Why\": \"The malformed nested <a> tags produced invalid HTML that could break tap targets on mobile, making it harder for mobile users to call or email—repairing it protects a key conversion path (phone orders).\", \"Hash\": \"09ab34ce\"}]}","refusal":null,"reasoning":"I'm planning to improve the gift cards category page for conversion — better SEO title/meta, a stronger header explaining instant delivery and non-expiring benefits, trust signals, reordering products by price, and fixing a mobile menu nested anchor bug.\n\nI'll also add a benefits bar with icons, a \"Most Popular\" badge on the $50 card, updated CTA text like \"Buy Gift Card,\" and a reassurance/FAQ section below the products, working directly with the provided HTML rather than fetching the URL.\n\nI'm finalizing the full changelog: SEO title/meta, category intro copy, a trust/benefit bar, reordering products low-to-high with a \"Most Popular\" badge on $50, swapping \"Free Shipping\" 