d. Theme by <a href=\\\"https://www.tangopixel.com/\\\">TangoPixel.</a></p>\\n                </div>\\n            </div>\\n        </div>\\n    </footer>\\n\\n    <nav id=\\\"mobile-menu\\\" class=\\\"mobile-menu\\\">\\n        <div class=\\\"mobile-menu-inner\\\">\\n            <div class=\\\"mobile-menu-close\\\">\\n                <a href=\\\"#\\\"></a>\\n            </div>\\n            <div class=\\\"mobile-menu-widget category-widget\\\">\\n                <h3>Categories</h3>\\n                <div id=\\\"mobile-categories\\\"></div>\\n            </div>\\n            <div class=\\\"mobile-menu-widget\\\">\\n                <h3>Menu Links</h3>\\n                <div id=\\\"mobile-menulinks\\\"></div>\\n            </div>\\n            <div class=\\\"mobile-menu-widget last-widget\\\">\\n                <div class=\\\"ContactInfo\\\">                    \\n                    <span><a href=\\\"tel:+18003318233\\\">Call Us</a> / <a href=\\\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#87e4f2f4f3e8eae2f5f4e2f5f1eee4e2c7fee8e0e6e3eef5e2e4f3a9e4e8ea\\\">Mail us</a></span>                     \\n                </div>\\n                <div class=\\\"account-links\\\">\\n                    <a href=\\\"myaccount.asp\\\"> Login</a> / <a href=\\\"register.asp\\\"> Register</a>\\n                </div>\\n            </div>\\n        </div>\\n    </nav>\\n\\n    <!--START: quickview_modal-->\\n    <aside id=\\\"qv-modal\\\" class=\\\"qv qv-modal modal\\\" tabindex=\\\"-1\\\" role=\\\"dialog\\\" data-catalogid=\\\"\\\" data-price=\\\"0\\\" data-sku=\\\"\\\" data-backdrop=\\\"true\\\">\\n\\t<div class=\\\"modal-dialog\\\" role=\\\"document\\\">\\n\\t\\t<div class=\\\"modal-vcenter\\\">\\n\\t\\t\\t<div class=\\\"qv-loader\\\">\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t<span class=\\\"mailing-btn-load icon-spin2 animate-spin\\\"></span>\\n\\t\\t\\t</div>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t<div class=\\\"product-item modal-content\\\">\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t<button type=\\\"button\\\" class=\\\"qv-close close\\\" data-dismiss=\\\"modal\\\" aria-label=\\\"Close\\\"><span aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\">&times;</span></button>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t<iframe id=\\\"qvIframe\\\" frameborder=\\\"0\\\"></iframe>\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t</div>\\n\\t\\t</div>\\n\\t</div>\\n</aside>\\n\\n    <!--END: quickview_modal-->\\n\\n    <link href=\\\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Lato:300,400,700\\\" rel=\\\"stylesheet\\\">\\n    <link href=\\\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Roboto+Condensed:400,700\\\" rel=\\\"stylesheet\\\">\\n    <link href=\\\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Playfair+Display:400,400i,700,700i\\\" rel=\\\"stylesheet\\\">\\n\\t<link rel=\\\"StyleSheet\\\" href=\\\"assets/templates/common-core/lib/fontello/css/fontello.min.css?vcart=26.37.3\\\" type=\\\"text/css\\\" />\\n    <link rel=\\\"StyleSheet\\\" href=\\\"assets/templates/common-core/lib/fontello/css/animation.css?vcart=26.37.3\\\" type=\\\"text/css\\\" />\\n\\t<link rel=\\\"StyleSheet\\\" href=\\\"assets/templates/my-mimosa-core-premium/css/line-awesome.css?vcart=26.37.3\\\" type=\\\"text/css\\\" />\\n    \\n\\t<!--START: page_scripts-->\\n    <!--<script src=\\\"https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/1.11.3/jquery.min.js\\\"></script>-->\\n\\t<script data-cfasync=\\\"false\\\" src=\\\"/cdn-cgi/scripts/5c5dd728/cloudflare-static/email-decode.min.js\\\"></script><script src='assets/templates/common-core/lib/jquery.min.js?vcart=26.37.3'></script>\\n    <script src=\\\"assets/templates/common-core/lib/bootstrap/js/bootstrap.js?vcart=26.37.3\\\"></script>\\n    <script src=\\\"assets/templates/common-core/js/core.js?vcart=26.37.3\\\"></script>\\n    <script src=\\\"assets/templates/my-mimosa-core-premium/js/main.js?vcart=26.37.3\\\"></script>\\n\\t\\n\\n\\n\\t<!--END: page_scripts-->\\n\\n    <!--START: quicksearch-->\\n    <link rel=\\\"stylesheet\\\" href=\\\"assets/templates/common-core/quicksearch/quicksearch.css?vcart=26.37.3\\\" type=\\\"text/css\\\" media=\\\"screen\\\" />\\n    <script type=\\\"text/javascript\\\" src=\\\"assets/templates/common-core/quicksearch/jquery.quicksearch.js?vcart=26.37.3\\\"></script>\\n    <script type=\\\"text/javascript\\\">\\n        jQuery(function () {\\n            jQuery('#searchlight').searchlight('/search_quick.asp');\\n        });\\n    </script>\\n    <!--END: quicksearch-->\\n    <script src='//unpkg.com/scrollreveal@3.3.5/dist/scrollreveal.min.js'></script>\\n    <script>\\n    /*\\n    var freeship = 99;    \\n    var total = \\\"$0\\\";    \\n    var fsDiv = document.getElementById(\\\"frameFSMsg\\\");    \\n    var totalnum = total.replace(\\\"$\\\", \\\"\\\");    \\n    var strContent = \\\"\\\";\\t\\n    var viewCart = '<span class=\\\"v-c-section\\\"><a href=\\\"/view_cart.asp\\\">View Cart</a></span>';    \\n    if (totalnum < freeship) {      \\n        rounded = Math.round((freeship - totalnum) * 100) / 100;      \\n        strContent = \\\"You Are <span class=\\\\\\\"lime\\\\\\\" style=\\\\\\\"padding:0px;\\\\\\\">$\\\";      \\n        strContent = strContent + rounded.toFixed(2) + \\\" \\\";      \\n        strContent = strContent + \\\"</span> Away from Free Shipping\\\";    \\n    }else      \\n    strContent = \\\"Your Order Qualifies for Free Shipping!\\\";    \\n    fsDiv.innerHTML = strContent;0\\n    */\\n\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\n    $('.product-item .second_img').each(function(i){\\n        var imgSrc = this.src;\\n        if(imgSrc.indexOf('/default.jpg') >= 0){\\n            $(this).parent().parent().addClass('noSecond_Image');\\n        }\\n    });    \\n    window.sr = ScrollReveal({ reset: true });\\n    sr.reveal('.lazy', { \\n        duration: 1000,\\n        origin: 'bottom'\\n    });    \\n    jQuery(\\\"<a href='#'' class='scrollup'><i class='la la-angle-double-up'></i></a>\\\").appendTo(\\\"body\\\");\\n    jQuery(window).scroll(function(){\\n        if (jQuery(this).scrollTop() > 100) {\\n            jQuery('.scrollup').fadeIn();\\n        } else {\\n            jQuery('.scrollup').fadeOut();\\n        }\\n    });\\n    jQuery('.scrollup').click(function(){\\n        jQuery(\\\"html, body\\\").animate({ scrollTop: 0 }, 600);\\n        return false;\\n    });\\n    $(window).scroll(function(){\\n        if ($(window).scrollTop() >= 200) {\\n           $('#frameMsg').addClass('fixed-header');\\n           $('.navbar-wrapper').addClass('fixed-header');\\n           $('.site-header').addClass('fixed-mobheader');\\n           $('.content-holder').css(\\\"margin-top\\\",\\\"89px\\\");\\n           $('.frameMsgOff .content-holder').css(\\\"margin-top\\\",\\\"56px\\\");\\n        }\\n        else {\\n           $('#frameMsg').removeClass('fixed-header');\\n           $('.navbar-wrapper').removeClass('fixed-header');\\n           $('.site-header').removeClass('fixed-mobheader');\\n           $('.content-holder').css(\\\"margin-top\\\",\\\"0px\\\");\\n\\n        }\\n    });\\n    </script>\\n    \\n<script src=\\\"//code.tidio.co/rgocgttxgleaoklf4s8ihf7xi1ncj3oz.js\\\" async></script>\\n<script type=\\\"text/javascript\\\" async=\\\"\\\" src=\\\"https://static.klaviyo.com/onsite/js/klaviyo.js?company_id=XyXada\\\"></script>\\n<script type=\\\"text/javascript\\\">var _cart_secure_url = \\\"https://www.yogadirect.com\\\"</script>\\n<img src=\\\"_e/spx/v1/img/logo.png\\\"  width=\\\"0\\\" alt=\\\"Logo\\\" /><script>var refEncoded = encodeURIComponent(document.referrer);(new Image()).src = 'https://www.yogadirect.com/3dvisit.asp?setReferer='+refEncoded</script></body>\\n</html>\",\"improvements\":[{\"What\":\"Added a three-card \\\"contact choice\\\" hero at the top of the page (Call / Live Chat / Email) with tap-to-call number, business hours, a response-time expectation and clear CTA buttons.\",\"Why\":\"Contact pages convert on one thing: getting the visitor to make contact. Presenting the three channels as prominent, clickable cards above the fold removes the need to read a wall of text and gives mobile users a one-tap phone call, which is the highest-intent (and often highest-revenue) contact action.\",\"Hash\":\"hero-contact-cards\"},{\"What\":\"Fixed broken/incorrect contact links: local phone was href=\\\"18607683086\\\" (not a tel: link) and toll-free links contained a space (\\\"tel: 18003318233\\\"). All now use tel:+1800... / tel:+1860... formats, plus added a tel link in the footer and mobile menu.\",\"Why\":\"Broken phone links silently kill calls on mobile. Correct tel: formatting makes every phone number instantly dialable, directly recovering lost sales and support calls.\",\"Hash\":\"fix-tel-links\"},{\"What\":\"Added a mobile-only sticky bottom bar with \\\"Call Us\\\" and \\\"Email Us\\\" buttons (with page padding so it never covers content).\",\"Why\":\"Most contact-page traffic is mobile. A persistent CTA bar means the visitor can convert at any scroll depth instead of having to scroll back up, typically lifting contact/call rates significantly.\",\"Hash\":\"mobile-sticky-cta\"},{\"What\":\"Wired the Live Chat card to the existing Tidio widget (window.tidioChatApi.open()) with a graceful fallback that scrolls to the contact form, and added GA/Google Ads event tracking on calls, chat opens and form submits.\",\"Why\":\"The chat tool was already loaded but invisible as an option. Surfacing it deflects easy questions instantly (cheaper than email) and event tracking lets the store measure and optimize which contact path drives revenue.\",\"Hash\":\"chat-and-tracking\"},{\"What\":\"Added a \\\"Get your answer in seconds\\\" self-service tile grid linking to Track My Order, Shipping, Returns, FAQs, Bulk/Quantity Pricing, Custom Printing, Rewards and Deals.\",\"Why\":\"Deflects repetitive support tickets while routing visitors back into revenue pages (bulk pricing, custom printing, sale) instead of dead-ending them on a form.\",\"Hash\":\"self-service-tiles\"},{\"What\":\"Rebuilt the third-party EmailMeForm embed presentation: full-width responsive layout instead of a fixed 640px box, hidden vendor logo, stacked bold labels, large touch-friendly 16px inputs, focus states, and a full-width green \\\"Send My Message\\\" button; also added helpful placeholders, autocomplete/inputmode attributes and clearer department option labels (values untouched).\",\"Why\":\"Form friction is the #1 cause of contact-page abandonment. Larger fields, visible labels, mobile keyboards, and an action-oriented button label (\\\"Send My Message\\\" vs \\\"Submit\\\") measurably increase form completion — while leaving field names/values intact so submissions keep working.\",\"Hash\":\"form-ux-upgrade\"},{\"What\":\"Moved the contact form into a titled card with a note setting a reply expectation and asking for order number/name, plus an \\\"in a hurry, call us\\\" line below the submit button.\",\"Why\":\"Setting response expectations reduces abandonment and duplicate messages, and asking for order details up front means issues are solved on first reply (fewer round trips, faster refunds/replacements, happier repeat buyers).\",\"Hash\":\"form-card-framing\"},{\"What\":\"Added a trust strip (phone/email/chat support, hassle-free returns, quantity discounts, secure checkout) and a dedicated B2B band: \\\"Buying for a studio, school or team?\\\" with CTAs to Quantity Discounts, Custom Printing and Request a Quote.\",\"Why\":\"Contact pages get a lot of high-value wholesale/bulk and custom-logo enquiries. Explicitly inviting those requests and linking the relevant pages captures high-AOV orders that would otherwise never be asked for.\",\"Hash\":\"trust-and-b2b-cta\"},{\"What\":\"Converted the long informational text blocks (Order Status, Problems with an Order, Returns, Sales Questions, Shipping) into a scannable collapsible FAQ, fixed the broken \\\"?\\\" mojibake characters, and reorganized phone/email/hours/address into four clean detail cards with the returns warning highlighted.\",\"Why\":\"Scannable, accordion content gets read; walls of text get skipped. Clean typography and corrected characters also raise perceived professionalism, which correlates with willingness to buy.\",\"Hash\":\"faq-and-details\"},{\"What\":\"Added a closing \\\"While you're here — shop popular gear\\\" CTA band (Mats, Bolsters, Props, Kits & Bundles, Sale) and a quantity-discounts link in the footer.\",\"Why\":\"Gives the page a commercial exit path: visitors whose question was answered are pushed toward product pages instead of leaving, turning a pure cost page into a revenue contributor.\",\"Hash\":\"shop-exit-cta\"},{\"What\":\"SEO/technical: rewrote the title and meta description with the phone number, hours and channels; added Organization + ContactPoint JSON-LD with address and opening hours; added a supporting H1 subheading; removed duplicate role=\\\"main\\\" landmarks and improved the promo banner and search placeholder copy.\",\"Why\":\"Better click-through from search for \\\"yogadirect contact/phone number\\\" queries, eligibility for richer search results, and cleaner accessibility semantics — all of which increase qualified traffic reaching the page.\",\"Hash\":\"seo-schema-a11y\"}]}","refusal":null,"reasoning":"I'm reviewing the contact page to plan conversion-focused improvements—trust signals, FAQ links, click-to-call, live chat, better form styling, response time promises, and newsletter incentives—while preserving the existing structure and fixing the broken phone number.\n\nI also want to correct malformed characters, add a hero section with call/email/chat action cards, and build a \"quick answers\" area for order status, shipping, and returns to deflect support load. Before adding any trust claims, I should verify facts by fetching the contact-us page and the-direct-difference page rather than fabricating details.There's a discrepancy between the address in the given HTML (219 Turner Road) and what the live page seems to show (2919 West Leigh Street) — I'll trust the provided HTML's address since I shouldn't alter facts based on a possibly cached fetch. Now I'm planning to preserve all existing content while adding inline styles for new sections.\n\nFor the restructured content area, I'm sketching a hero section with three contact options — phone with hours, obfuscated email links kept as-is, and a live chat button tied into Tidio with email fallback. Below that I'm adding a softened response-time promise (\"aim to reply within 1 business day\") to avoid an overly strong guarantee, plus a self-service grid linking to order status, shipping, returns, FAQs, rewards, and quantity discounts to help with both support and conversion.\n\nI'm keeping the third-party emailmeform embed untouched internally but wrapping it in a nicer card, adding a heading, and overriding its fixed width with responsive full-width CSS and a larger submit button. I'm also planning revenue-focused additions: a wholesale/custom-printing quote CTA, a \"shop best sellers\" link row, a nod to the rewards program in place of a newsletter signup, a mobile-only sticky call/email bar, and trust elements like payment icons already in the footer — while being cautious about reintroducing an unverified free-shipping claim that's currently commented out in the header.\n\nI'm also planning SEO and accessibility fixes: better title/meta descriptions, LocalBusiness schema with phone/hours/address plus Organization ContactPoint schema, and cleaning up duplicate role=\"main\" attributes. For the form itself, I'll keep the department select's value attribute untouched to avoid breaking backend routing but trim the visible label text, and I'll avoid adding new fields like an order number since that could change the expected element count — instead I'll consider safe placeholder hints on existing inputs.\n\nI'll add helpful placeholder text and autocomplete attributes to the name, email, phone, subject, and message fields to improve completion, while leaving the recaptcha sitekey untouched. I'm also planning a mailto fallback link in case the form submission fails. Now I'm building the contact content block's HTML structure — a wrapping div with an intro paragraph, a row of help cards, and an assurance section with badges about response time and support availability.\n\nI'm avoiding overly specific claims like naming Virginia directly, opting instead for phrasing like \"Mon–Fri 9am–5pm EST\" and \"Phone, email & live chat support.\" I'm laying out a self-service grid linking to account, shipping, returns, FAQs, rewards, bulk discounts, and custom printing pages, followed by the contact form card, then preserving the original informational sections on order status, problems, returns, and sales questions in a \"more help\" area with contact details retained.\n\nI'm adding a bottom revenue-focused section promoting popular categories like mats, bolsters, props, and sale items, plus a note on quantity discounts, along with a mobile sticky bar with call and chat buttons that appears only on small screens. I also want to update the title and meta description for SEO before finalizing everything while keeping the scripts intact.\n\nWriting the chat button click handler...\n\nAdding CSS for the layout styling...\n\nSettling on a calm teal-green accent (#4a7c59) for the brand color, and defining button styles with bold uppercase text on that green background.\n\nAlso stripping the emf form's default styling entirely—removing borders, shadows, logo—and rebuilding the field layout to be full-width with clean labels and consistent input padding.\n\nSince the plugin's own stylesheet loads after mine, I'm making sure the override rules use !important on widths, floats, and label display so my styling actually wins, especially since the theme forces left-aligned labels via a specific class.\n\nNow I'm sketching a sticky mobile bar that's hidden by default and only appears as a flex layout on small screens.\n\nI'm keeping the sticky bar to just Call and Email buttons so it doesn't visually clash with the Tidio chat bubble sitting bottom-right, and planning to add Organization schema markup with contact point, address, and opening hours before assembling the complete page.\n\nI want to add a factual link about volume pricing for studios, schools, or gyms pointing to the existing quantity-discount page, plus a subheading under the H1 saying \"We're here to help\" for a friendlier tone. Now I'm ready to write out the final HTML carefully.\n\nI'm keeping the form markup essentially identical while writing an intro paragraph and contact cards -- one with a phone link and other help options for reaching customer service.\n\nAdding a live chat card...\n\nSince nested mailto anchors aren't valid, I'll put email addresses on a separate line beneath the cards instead, listing customer service and custom printing contacts. Then I'm adding a trust strip with checkmarks for real support, hassle-free returns, volume pricing, and secure checkout, followed by a self-serve answer grid.\n\nI'm laying out the self-serve cards linking to order tracking, shipping, returns, FAQs, rewards, bulk pricing, and custom printing pages, then adding a contact form section, followed by the original phone/email/hours/address details with corrected links, the existing long-form help text, and a closing \"Ready to shop?\" band linking to mats, bolsters, props, and sale pages. I'm keeping the original heading classes for style consistency while adding my own anchor ID for the form section.\n\nNow I need to structure the final JSON output with an improvements list including What/Why/Hash fields for each change, using brief slug-style identifiers as hashes, then write out the complete HTML carefully, making sure the department select keeps its original option values while trimming the \"Service\" label.","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm reviewing the contact page to plan conversion-focused improvements—trust signals, FAQ links, click-to-call, live chat, better form styling, response time promises, and newsletter incentives—while preserving the exi