s with bold uppercase text on that green background.\n\nAlso stripping the emf form's default styling entirely—removing borders, shadows, logo—and rebuilding the field layout to be full-width with clean labels and consistent input padding.\n\nSince the plugin's own stylesheet loads after mine, I'm making sure the override rules use !important on widths, floats, and label display so my styling actually wins, especially since the theme forces left-aligned labels via a specific class.\n\nNow I'm sketching a sticky mobile bar that's hidden by default and only appears as a flex layout on small screens.\n\nI'm keeping the sticky bar to just Call and Email buttons so it doesn't visually clash with the Tidio chat bubble sitting bottom-right, and planning to add Organization schema markup with contact point, address, and opening hours before assembling the complete page.\n\nI want to add a factual link about volume pricing for studios, schools, or gyms pointing to the existing quantity-discount page, plus a subheading under the H1 saying \"We're here to help\" for a friendlier tone. Now I'm ready to write out the final HTML carefully.\n\nI'm keeping the form markup essentially identical while writing an intro paragraph and contact cards -- one with a phone link and other help options for reaching customer service.\n\nAdding a live chat card...\n\nSince nested mailto anchors aren't valid, I'll put email addresses on a separate line beneath the cards instead, listing customer service and custom printing contacts. Then I'm adding a trust strip with checkmarks for real support, hassle-free returns, volume pricing, and secure checkout, followed by a self-serve answer grid.\n\nI'm laying out the self-serve cards linking to order tracking, shipping, returns, FAQs, rewards, bulk pricing, and custom printing pages, then adding a contact form section, followed by the original phone/email/hours/address details with corrected links, the existing long-form help text, and a closing \"Ready to shop?\" band linking to mats, bolsters, props, and sale pages. I'm keeping the original heading classes for style consistency while adding my own anchor ID for the form section.\n\nNow I need to structure the final JSON output with an improvements list including What/Why/Hash fields for each change, using brief slug-style identifiers as hashes, then write out the complete HTML carefully, making sure the department select keeps its original option values while trimming the \"Service\" label.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":1,"signature":""}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":48921,"completion_tokens":44633,"total_tokens":93554,"cost":1.36043,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":1.36043,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.244605,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":1.115825},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":5827,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0},"server_tool_use_details":{"web_search_requests":0}}}
