\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\thasAdvancedOptions=false;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\tcatch(e){\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif (e.name.toString() == 'ReferenceError' ){\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\thasAdvancedOptions=false;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\tif(hasAdvancedOptions){\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tid=target.data().relHookdataId;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcontent_type=\\\"product_group\\\"\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\telse{\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tid=sku;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcontent_type=\\\"product\\\"\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\tif(pos==0){\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tids=\\\"'\\\"+id+\\\"'\\\";\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcurrency = target.data().relHookdataCurrency;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\telse{\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tids=ids+\\\",\\\"+\\\"'\\\"+id+\\\"'\\\";\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\tvar price = target.data().relHookdataPrice;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\ttotal+=parseFloat(price);\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\tpos = pos + 1;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n});\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\ntotal = total.toFixed(2);\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\nif(ids!=\\\"\\\"){\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\tids = \\\"[\\\"+ids+\\\"]\\\";\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\tfbq('track', 'ViewContent', {\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\tcontent_ids: ids,\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\tcontent_type: content_type,\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\tvalue: total,\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\tcurrency: currency\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t});\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n</script>\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n<noscript>\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n<img height='1' width='1' style='display:none' src='https://www.facebook.com/tr?id=731885793537364&ev=ViewContent&noscript=1' />\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n</noscript>\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t</body>\\n</html>\",\"improvements\":[{\"What\":\"Rewrote the page header: new H1 \\\"Yoga Gift Cards\\\", a benefit-led intro paragraph and a four-item benefit bar (instant email delivery, never expires/no fees, use on 1,000+ products, secure checkout).\",\"Why\":\"The original page showed only the bare word \\\"Gift Cards\\\" with no value proposition or reassurance. Gift-card buyers are anxious about delivery speed, expiration and fees; answering those objections above the fold is the single biggest lever on gift-card conversion.\",\"Hash\":\"page_header\"},{\"What\":\"Reordered products low-to-high ($25 → $50 → $100), added decision badges (\\\"Great starter gift\\\", \\\"Most popular\\\" with a highlighted border, \\\"Best for a full setup\\\") and a short \\\"what this buys\\\" blurb under each price.\",\"Why\":\"An anchored, clearly differentiated ladder reduces choice paralysis and nudges buyers toward the mid/high denominations, lifting average order value. Concrete \\\"covers a mat + block\\\" framing makes the abstract dollar amount tangible.\",\"Hash\":\"product_tiles\"},{\"What\":\"Made CTAs specific and full-width (\\\"Send a $50 Gift Card\\\" instead of generic \\\"Add To Cart\\\") and added a micro-copy line \\\"⚡ Delivered by email in minutes\\\" directly under each button.\",\"Why\":\"Action-specific button text converts better than generic \\\"Add To Cart\\\", and the delivery reassurance sits exactly at the moment of hesitation (click), removing the main last-minute-gift objection.\",\"Hash\":\"cta_copy\"},{\"What\":\"Relabeled the product badges for digital goods: \\\"Free Shipping\\\" → \\\"Emailed Free\\\" and \\\"In Stock\\\" → \\\"Ready to Send\\\".\",\"Why\":\"\\\"Free shipping / In stock\\\" on an e-gift card is confusing and can imply a physical card that must arrive by mail, creating doubt about timing.\",\"Hash\":\"badges_digital\"},{\"What\":\"Added a trust strip, a \\\"How it works\\\" 3-step section and an on-page FAQ (delivery time, expiration/fees, what it can be used on, combining payments, sending to someone else's email) with FAQPage schema markup.\",\"Why\":\"Handles the top pre-purchase objections without forcing the visitor to leave for a help page, and the structured data can earn FAQ rich results, increasing organic click-through to this commercial page.\",\"Hash\":\"trust_faq\"},{\"What\":\"Added a bulk/corporate gift-card block (studios, teams, events) with click-to-call, contact and quantity-pricing CTAs, plus a note about ordering multiple cards or custom amounts by phone.\",\"Why\":\"Bulk and corporate gifting orders are high-value; surfacing them on the gift-card page captures revenue that would otherwise bounce because only three fixed amounts are listed.\",\"Hash\":\"bulk_block\"},{\"What\":\"Replaced the generic sale banner message on this page with a gift-relevant promise that anchor-links to the product grid, and added a mobile-only sticky \\\"Choose a Gift Card Amount\\\" bar with smooth-scroll behaviour.\",\"Why\":\"Keeps intent-matched messaging instead of pushing gift shoppers into a sale category, and gives mobile users a persistent path back to the buying decision, which typically lifts mobile add-to-cart rate.\",\"Hash\":\"banner_sticky\"},{\"What\":\"Improved the SEO title and meta description (\\\"Yoga Gift Cards | Instant Email Delivery\\\" plus benefit-rich description) and retitled the grid heading to \\\"Choose your gift amount\\\" with supporting sub-copy instead of \\\"Products [3]\\\".\",\"Why\":\"A benefit-loaded title/description raises SERP click-through for gift-related queries, and an instructional heading tells visitors exactly what to do next rather than reporting an inventory count of only three items.\",\"Hash\":\"seo_headings\"}]}","refusal":null,"reasoning":"I should check the actual page to ground my improvements, but I can also focus directly on conversion tactics: stronger header copy emphasizing value props like no expiration, instant delivery, no fees, and sitewide redemption, plus reordering the gift card amounts ascending for clarity.\n\nI'm also thinking about adding trust signals and objection-handling elements — FAQ accordion with structured data, delivery/urgency messaging (\"delivered instantly by email\"), swapping irrelevant \"Free Shipping\" badges for \"Instant Email Delivery,\" and updating CTA copy to something like \"Buy & Send Now.\" To boost AOV, I want to highlight the $100 card as best value with a suggested use case, and maybe add an email capture for a discount code, all styled with inline CSS so the page doesn't depend on external stylesheets.\n\nNow I'm reordering the product cards ($25, $50 marked \"Most Popular\", $100) and adding a fourth \"Custom Amount\" card linking to the gift-certificates page, plus value messaging under each price. I also want a benefits-icon hero band, a \"How it works\" 3-step section, an FAQ with schema markup, and a bulk/corporate gift card CTA with a phone number for studios ordering 10+, all while preserving the existing tracking scripts and JS untouched.\n\nI'm updating the page title and meta description to be more gift-card focused, adding an e-gift benefits bar in the header, and swapping the \"Free Shipping\" badge for \"Instant Delivery\" messaging on each card.\n\nI'm also revising the CTA button text to \"Buy Gift Card\" while keeping the existing ajax cart classes, and drafting CSS for the hero, benefits, steps, FAQ, bulk, and badge sections. I'm also considering updating the site-wide promo banner to highlight instant, no-expiration eGift cards instead of the generic discount message.\n\nWriting hero styles and benefits list...\n\nNow planning the product tiles for the gift card amounts—$25 as a starter option and $50 as the most popular pick—along with the \"How it works\" section, corporate/bulk box, and FAQ schema markup, plus renaming the products section title to \"Choose your gift amount.\"\n\nThen $100 as best value, and rethinking the fourth tile: instead of another fixed price, I want it to be a non-product card for bulk/corporate gifting with contact options like phone and email, since a custom-amount link would be confusing next to the fixed product URLs.\n\nI'll leave the script placement order as-is since it's just collection assignment and doesn't affect functionality, then focus on adding FAQ JSON-LD to the body before writing the final version.","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I should check the actual page to ground my improvements, but I can also focus directly on conversion tactics: stronger header copy emphasizing value props like no expiration, instant delivery, no fees, and sitewide redemption, plus reordering the gift card amounts ascending for clarity.\n\nI'm also thinking about adding trust signals and objection-handling elements — FAQ accordion with structured data, delivery/urgency messaging (\"delivered instantly by email\"), swapping irrelevant \"Free Shipping\" badges for \"Instant Email Delivery,\" and updating CTA copy to something like \"Buy & Send Now.\" To boost AOV, I want to highlight the $100 card as best value with a suggested use case, and maybe add an email capture for a discount code, all styled with inline CSS so the page doesn't depend on external stylesheets.\n\nNow I'm reordering the product cards ($25, $50 marked \"Most Popular\", $100) and adding a fourth \"Custom Amount\" card linking to the gift-certificates page, plus value messaging under each price. I also want a benefits-icon hero band, a \"How it works\" 3-step section, an FAQ with schema markup, and a bulk/corporate gift card CTA with a phone number for studios ordering 10+, all while preserving the existing tracking scripts and JS untouched.\n\nI'm updating the page title and meta description to be more gift-card focused, adding an e-gift benefits bar in the header, and swapping the \"Free Shipping\" badge for \"Instant Delivery\" messaging on each card.\n\nI'm also revising the CTA button text to \"Buy Gift Card\" while keeping the existing ajax cart classes, and drafting CSS for the hero, benefits, steps, FAQ, bulk, and badge sections. I'm also considering updating the site-wide promo banner to highlight instant, no-expiration eGift cards instead of the generic discount message.\n\nWriting hero styles and benefits list...\n\nNow planning the product tiles for the gift card amounts—$25 as a starter option and $50 as the most popular pick—along with the \"How it works\" section, corporate/bulk box, and FAQ schema markup, plus renaming the products section title to \"Choose your gift amount.\"\n\nThen $100 as best value, and rethinking the fourth tile: instead of another fixed price, I want it to be a non-product card for bulk/corporate gifting with contact options like phone and email, since a custom-amount link would be confusing next to the fixed product URLs.\n\nI'll leave the script placement order as-is since it's just collection assignment and doesn't affect functionality, then focus on adding FAQ JSON-LD to the body before writing the final version.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":""}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":19173,"completion_tokens":33043,"total_tokens":52216,"cost":0.92194,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.92194,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.095865,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.826075},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2477,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}
