\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tid=target.data().relHookdataId;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcontent_type=\\\"product_group\\\"\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\telse{\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tid=sku;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcontent_type=\\\"product\\\"\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\tif(pos==0){\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tids=\\\"'\\\"+id+\\\"'\\\";\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcurrency = target.data().relHookdataCurrency;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\telse{\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tids=ids+\\\",\\\"+\\\"'\\\"+id+\\\"'\\\";\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\tvar price = target.data().relHookdataPrice;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\ttotal+=parseFloat(price);\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\tpos = pos + 1;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n});\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\ntotal = total.toFixed(2);\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\nif(ids!=\\\"\\\"){\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\tids = \\\"[\\\"+ids+\\\"]\\\";\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\tfbq('track', 'ViewContent', {\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\tcontent_ids: ids,\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\tcontent_type: content_type,\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\tvalue: total,\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\tcurrency: currency\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t});\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n</script>\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n<noscript>\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n<img height='1' width='1' style='display:none' src='https://www.facebook.com/tr?id=731885793537364&ev=ViewContent&noscript=1' />\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n</noscript>\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t</body>\\n</html>\",\"improvements\":[{\"What\":\"Added a value-proposition trust bar directly under the header (wholesale pricing, trusted by studios since 1998, individually wrapped/unbranded, quantity discounts, custom logo printing) and enriched the three store-message tiles with explicit click-through cues.\",\"Why\":\"Category pages lose visitors who don't know why to buy\"}]}","refusal":null,"reasoning":"I'm considering whether to fetch the live page for reference, but since the HTML is already provided, I'll skip that and focus directly on improving the conversion.\n\nI'm sketching out concrete changes: a stronger value-prop banner referencing free shipping over $99, a trust bar noting they've served studios since 1998, upgraded product cards with savings badges and clearer out-of-stock states, better button copy like \"Choose Color,\" and quick filter chips for thickness and price.\n\nI'm also planning a client-side filtering system with chips like \"All,\" \"On Sale,\" \"In Stock,\" and \"Under $25,\" keeping the existing sort form intact rather than adding risky instant sorting. Beyond that, I want to add a concise buying guide comparing mat thicknesses, a bulk/wholesale CTA aimed at studios, and a newsletter signup offering a discount to grow the empty maillist.\n\nFor the email capture, I'm second-guessing whether to promise a specific discount since that's not authorized, so I'll frame it as \"exclusive deals\" instead. I'm also unsure about the exact form endpoint for their mailing list signup on Shift4Shop, so I'm weighing whether to include a form pointing to a likely endpoint or skip it in favor of a safer trust-building footer element.\n\nBeyond that, I'm thinking through smaller fixes: skipping a sticky mobile CTA since it's not needed here, adding safe microcopy like \"In Stock — ready to ship\" instead of unverified urgency claims, mentioning quantity pricing where it actually exists, and fixing the broken subcategory tile markup where the list isn't properly closed.\n\nNow I'm considering adding \"Best Seller\" and \"Top Rated\" badges based on actual review counts and ratings, and reordering the product grid so out-of-stock items move to the bottom rather than cluttering the top — swapping their CTA to \"View Details\" instead of a broken add-to-cart action.\n\nI'm also planning smaller additions: a thickness comparison guide near the top, an FAQ accordion with schema markup for SEO, and stronger phone CTA visibility for studio orders, plus a scoped inline style block so new elements don't clash with the existing theme, and a refined meta title/description with the free-shipping benefit worked in.\n\nWriting scoped CSS...\n\nI'm setting up JS filtering by adding data attributes for price, stock, and sale status onto each product item, then wiring up chip clicks to show/hide matching items, while leaving the existing server-side sort dropdown intact.\n\nI'm also refining button labels like \"Choose Options\" versus \"Add To Cart,\" checking that quick-add links still route to the product page for items with variants, and manually computing discount percentages for each sale item to display accurate \"Save X%\" badges.\n\nI'll mark \"Top Rated ★\" for items with 5-star ratings and enough reviews. For trust-building copy, I want to avoid fabricating numbers, so I'll use general statements like \"Trusted by studios, gyms & spas since 1998\" instead of unverified stats. I should verify the free shipping threshold by checking the actual shipping page before including that claim.I can't verify a specific shipping threshold, so I should avoid making that claim and instead stick to messaging already supported by the existing page copy — things like \"wholesale prices,\" \"trusted since 1998,\" \"individually wrapped & unbranded,\" and \"quantity pricing\" that I know are legitimate.\n\nNow I'm planning the full rebuild: sharpen the title and meta description, update the top banner with a supported discount claim, add a USP bar, restructure the category header into a concise intro with bullets and a collapsible section preserving the original SEO text, add thickness guide cards, a bulk/studio CTA, filter chips with JS, and product cards.\n\nI'm working through remaining sections — badges, stock handling, a FAQ accordion with schema, a footer newsletter form using the standard Shift4Shop mailinglist subscribe endpoint, a sticky bulk-order help bar with phone number, and cleanup of the subcategory tile markup.\n\nI'll fix the unclosed list in the subcategory grid, add lazy loading to product images past the first few for performance, and now I'm starting on the CSS for USP bar styling and layout.\n\nAdding guide grid styles...\n\nAdding badge styles...\n\nI'm also weighing whether to remove the existing on-sale badge span to avoid duplicating it with my new top-left badge system.\n\nDeciding to keep the on-sale badge with updated \"Save X%\" text, reserving corner badges only for Best Seller, Top Rated, and Out of Stock labels to reduce clutter. For out-of-stock items I'm dimming the image and swapping the CTA for a \"View Details\" link, plus adding a result count display like \"Showing X of 21\". Now I'm planning the filter chip JavaScript—clicking a chip toggles active state, loops through items to show/hide based on the filter, updates the count, and displays a \"none found\" message when nothing matches.\n\nWriting filter JS logic...\n\nI'm also considering that the product grid likely uses floats with column clearing, so hiding items via display:none could leave gaps; switching the container to flexbox with wrapping and giving each item a fixed percentage width should keep the layout clean even as items are filtered out, with a responsive breakpoint for smaller screens.\n\nAdding padding and flex-column styling so the action buttons stick to the bottom of each card regardless of content height, while making sure this doesn't interfere with the quickview overlay inside the image. I'm also planning to tweak the header banner text and consider an FAQ section using accordion-style JS.\n\nI'm drafting FAQ questions covering material thickness, cleaning, custom printing/logos, bulk pricing, and returns, keeping answers generic and pointing to relevant pages rather than citing specific numbers. I've also worked out the final product ordering—18 in-stock items followed by 3 out-of-stock ones, totaling 21—and I'm making sure each product's script tag stays properly paired with its div.\n\nFor badges, I'm reconsidering claims like \"Best Seller\" or \"Most Popular\" since those would be fabrications not backed by data; instead I'm sticking to factual labels like \"Top Rated\" for items with strong ratings, \"Out of Stock,\" and \"Bundle & Save\" where applicable.\n\nNow I'm working out the data attributes to attach to each product item for price, sale, and stock state, and planning the filter counts for the category list.\n\nWriting filter JS...\n\nI also want to update the visible product count element and restructure the page header, using a details/summary element for expandable copy and a count-aware H1 heading.\n\nI'm mapping thickness-guide cards to their real product URLs — travel/light cushion, all-purpose, extra cushion, extra long/wide, and eco/natural rubber mats — plus adding a custom printing link.\n\nSince JSON strings can't contain literal newlines and the scripts include `//` line comments that would break if concatenated, I need to escape actual newlines as \\n throughout the HTML output rather than flattening everything onto one line.\n\nFor the \"improvements\" array, I'll fill in short identifying strings for the Hash field using brief snippets tied to each change location, then move on to drafting the modified product card template for item 2421.\n\nI'm figuring out the badge structure — moving the \"Save 15%\" text to the corner badge and removing the redundant sale-badge span near the price, keeping the strikethrough and sale price intact. For out-of-stock items, I'm adding a corner \"Out of Stock\" badge and swapping the action button to a \"View Details\" link instead of add-to-cart.\n\nI need custom CSS for that out-of-stock button since the theme's default styling probably won't apply, and I'm sorting out which products get eco-related badges versus discount badges versus bundle labels, capping each product at two badges max.\n\nI'm finishing the badge assignments across the remaining products, mixing sale percentages, Top Rated, and OOS tags where relevant. Now I'm updating the cart button copy to \"Choose Options\" and \"Add To Cart\" with proper aria-labels, then moving on to write the newsletter block.\n\nWriting newsletter form markup...\n\nI'll skip the sticky trust badge near add-to-cart, but I'll polish the three store-messages blocks (Rewards Program, Quantity Pricing, Kits & Bundles) with clearer benefit copy and a \"Learn more\" arrow, then finalize everything.","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm considering whether to fetch the live page for reference, but since the HTML is already provided, I'll skip that and focus directly on improving the conversion.\n\nI'm sketching out concrete changes: a stronger value-prop banner referencing free shipping over $99, a trust bar noting they've served studios since 1998, upgraded p