t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\telse\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t{\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\thasAdvancedOptions=false;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\tcatch(e){\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif (e.name.toString() == 'ReferenceError' ){\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\thasAdvancedOptions=false;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\tif(hasAdvancedOptions){\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tid=target.data().relHookdataId;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcontent_type=\\\"product_group\\\"\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\telse{\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tid=sku;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcontent_type=\\\"product\\\"\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\tif(pos==0){\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tids=\\\"'\\\"+id+\\\"'\\\";\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcurrency = target.data().relHookdataCurrency;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\telse{\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tids=ids+\\\",\\\"+\\\"'\\\"+id+\\\"'\\\";\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\tvar price = target.data().relHookdataPrice;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\ttotal+=parseFloat(price);\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\tpos = pos + 1;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n});\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\ntotal = total.toFixed(2);\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\nif(ids!=\\\"\\\"){\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\tids = \\\"[\\\"+ids+\\\"]\\\";\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\tfbq('track', 'ViewContent', {\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\tcontent_ids: ids,\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\tcontent_type: content_type,\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\tvalue: total,\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\tcurrency: currency\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t});\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n</script>\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n<noscript>\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n<img height='1' width='1' style='display:none' src='https://www.facebook.com/tr?id=731885793537364&ev=ViewContent&noscript=1' />\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n</noscript>\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t</body>\\n</html>\",\"improvements\":[{\"What\":\"Replaced the vague announcement bar text with a concrete shipping incentive (\\\"FREE SHIPPING ON ORDERS $99+\\\") alongside the existing sale link.\",\"Why\":\"A specific, benefit-led offer in the highest-visibility slot on the page reduces shipping-cost anxiety (the #1 cause of cart abandonment) and gives visitors a reason to keep browsing rather than bounce.\",\"Hash\":\"promo-bar\"},{\"What\":\"Added a site-wide trust bar directly under the header messages: free shipping threshold, hassle-free returns, secure checkout, everyday low prices and a clickable phone number.\",\"Why\":\"Repeating risk-reversal and credibility signals above the product grid raises confidence for first-time visitors on an unfamiliar store, which lifts add-to-cart rates; the tap-to-call link also captures high-intent phone orders.\",\"Hash\":\"trust-bar\"},{\"What\":\"Added an intro paragraph beneath the H1 that explains what a \\\"specialty\\\" mat is, confirms stock availability and restates the free-shipping offer.\",\"Why\":\"Category pages with only 4 products convert poorly when they give no context. Framing the selection sets expectations, answers 'why buy here', and adds unique indexable copy for SEO traffic.\",\"Hash\":\"cat-intro\"},{\"What\":\"Added a row of pill-style quick links to related mat collections (Classic, Premium, Kids, Bags, Accessories, All Mats, Sale).\",\"Why\":\"With only four items, many shoppers hit a dead end. Giving instant paths to adjacent inventory keeps sessions alive, reduces exits, and increases the chance of finding a purchasable product.\",\"Hash\":\"quick-links\"},{\"What\":\"Enhanced product cards with corner badges (Save 15%, 68% Off – Clearance, Eco-Friendly), explicit dollar-savings lines, and an \\\"In stock & ready to ship\\\" reassurance under each CTA.\",\"Why\":\"Quantified savings and scarcity/urgency cues make discounts feel concrete and increase click-through to the product page; stock/shipping reassurance at the point of action removes the last hesitation before adding to cart.\",\"Hash\":\"card-badges\"},{\"What\":\"Clarified review count wording ((3 reviews)) and tightened CTA labels.\",\"Why\":\"Explicit social proof labelling is more persuasive than an ambiguous number, and clearer CTA wording sets accurate expectations about what happens next, reducing drop-off.\",\"Hash\":\"cta-reviews\"},{\"What\":\"Added two cross-sell panels below the grid: studio/bulk quantity pricing and yoga kits & bundles, each with a strong button CTA.\",\"Why\":\"These route shoppers to higher-AOV offers that already exist on the site (quantity discounts and bundles), directly increasing average order value and capturing studio/wholesale demand.\",\"Hash\":\"cross-sell\"},{\"What\":\"Added a 'need help choosing?' assistance block with phone and contact links.\",\"Why\":\"Considered purchases like mats stall on spec questions; offering human help converts otherwise-lost visitors and supports higher-value phone/email orders.\",\"Hash\":\"help-block\"},{\"What\":\"Added an accordion FAQ (thickness guidance, kids' mats, shipping cost, returns, custom printing) plus matching FAQPage structured data, and an 'About Our Specialty Yoga Mats' SEO paragraph with internal links.\",\"Why\":\"Pre-empting purchase objections on the category page removes friction before the product page, while the schema and unique copy can win rich results and more qualified organic traffic.\",\"Hash\":\"faq-seo\"},{\"What\":\"Made the sort-by dropdown auto-submit on change, and added a searchbox placeholder that communicates catalog breadth.\",\"Why\":\"Removing the hidden extra step in sorting prevents interaction dead-ends, and a descriptive search placeholder encourages use of site search, a behaviour strongly correlated with conversion.\",\"Hash\":\"ux-sort-search\"},{\"What\":\"Added 'Studio & Bulk Pricing' to the top utility nav and footer, and a secure-checkout note next to payment icons.\",\"Why\":\"Surfacing the bulk-pricing path globally captures the highest-AOV segment, while the security line near payment logos reinforces checkout trust at the point of decision.\",\"Hash\":\"nav-footer-trust\"}]}","refusal":null,"reasoning":"I'll do a quick fetch of the page to confirm its current styling before making improvements, then start listing out the changes I want to make, beginning with the category section.\n\nI'm planning to add trust badges, a sharper promo bar, urgency/scarcity elements, review stars, subcategory links, an email capture with a discount, improved product card CTAs showing savings, an FAQ section with schema, and free shipping messaging tied to the $99 threshold I noticed in the commented-out JS. Now I'm working through constructing the improved HTML with these new components layered in via inline styles.\n\nI'm firming up the announcement bar copy, adding a trust bar and header intro, and enhancing product cards with \"You Save $X\" savings badges rather than making unverified discount promises in the email signup -- instead I'll frame that around the existing rewards program. I'm now calculating specific savings percentages for each product to display as badges.\n\nI want to keep any added labels factual rather than fabricated, so I'll stick with things already true in the data like \"In Stock\" and \"Save 68%\" instead of invented urgency claims. I'm also planning to add a subcategory tile row for navigation since that section is currently empty, plus breadcrumbs and possibly FAQ/schema markup to strengthen SEO.\n\nSince the final output has to be a single-line JSON string, I need to be meticulous about escaping all quotes within the HTML I'm generating -- that's going to require careful attention across a long block of markup.\n\nThen I'm updating the announcement bar to promote free shipping and sale link, and adding a trust bar beneath the store-messages div with icons for shipping and returns, though I'm second-guessing the returns claim since the policy details aren't confirmed.\n\nContinuing the trust bar, I swap in safer copy avoiding specific dates, then plan additions for the page header intro, subcategory links, and product card upgrades—savings badges, trust microcopy, and more actionable CTA text like \"Choose Options →.\"  After the products I'll add a value prop section, quantity discount banner, FAQ, and newsletter signup, plus JSON-LD FAQ markup alongside the existing breadcrumb microdata. Writing trust bar CSS...\n\nAdding hover states, a savings badge style, and a shipping note element for the value props section.\n\nSince the newsletter form target is empty and risky to fake, I decide to replace it with a CTA panel linking to existing pages like the Rewards Program and Quantity Pricing instead of a fake mailing-list form. I'll also leave reviews blank for items without any, and add lazy-loading attributes for images.\n\nI'm skipping fabricated ratings and free shipping progress since there's no real data to back them up, but I'll add \"You may also like\" links using the existing quicklinks categories, and add a percentage overlay badge on sale images.\n\nAdding overlay badge styles...\n\nFor item 2179 I'll show \"68% OFF\" and for item 2509 \"15% OFF,\" keeping the quickview button positioning intact. I'm structuring the improvements array with What/Why entries and short descriptive identifiers instead of real hashes, then drafting the full HTML section by section before finalizing the JSON output.\n\nI'm deciding to leave the CTA button text mostly as-is, maybe adding a small shipping note beneath \"Add To Cart\" rather than altering the arrow styling, and skipping the mobile sticky footer promo idea. Now I'm ready to write out the final answer.","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'll do a quick fetch of the page to confirm its current styling before making improvements, then start listing out the changes I want to make, beginning with the category section.\n\nI'm planning to add trust badges, a sharper promo bar, urgency/scarcity elements, review stars, subcategory links, an email capture with a discount, improved product card CTAs showing savings, an FAQ section with schema, and free shipping messaging tied to the $99 threshold I noticed in the commented-out JS. Now I'm working through constructing the improved HTML with these new components layered in via inline styles.\n\nI'm firming up the announcement bar copy, adding a trust bar and header intro, and enhancing product cards with \"You Save $X\" savings badges rather than making unverified discount promises in the email signup -- instead I'll frame that around the existing rewards program. I'm now calculating specific savings percentages for each product to display as badges.\n\nI want to keep any added labels factual rather than fabricated, so I'll stick with things already true in the data like \"In Stock\" and \"Save 68%\" instead of invented urgency claims. I'm also planning to add a subcategory tile row for navigation since that section is currently empty, plus breadcrumbs and possibly FAQ/schema markup to strengthen SEO.\n\nSince the final output has to be a single-line JSON string, I need to be meticulous about escaping all quotes within the HTML I'm generating -- that's going to require careful attention across a long block of markup.\n\nThen I'm updating the announcement bar to promote free shipping and sale link, and adding a trust bar beneath the store-messages div with icons for shipping and returns, though I'm second-guessing the returns claim since the policy details aren't confirmed.\n\nContinuing the trust bar, I swap in safer copy avoiding specific dates, then plan additions for the page header intro, subcategory links, and product card upgrades—savings badges, trust microcopy, and more actionable CTA text like \"Choose Options →.\"  After the products I'll add a value prop section, quantity discount banner, FAQ, and newsletter signup, plus JSON-LD FAQ markup alongside the existing breadcrumb microdata. Writing trust bar CSS...\n\nAdding hover states, a savings badge style, and a shipping note element for the value props section.\n\nSince the newsletter form target is empty and risky to fake, I decide to replace it with a CTA panel linking to existing pages like the Rewards Program and Quantity Pricing instead of a fake mailing-list form. I'll also leave reviews blank for items without any, and add lazy-loading attributes for images.\n\nI'm skipping fabricated ratings and free shipping progress since there's no real data to back them up, but I'll add \"You may also like\" links using the existing quicklinks categories, and add a percentage overlay badge on sale images.\n\nAdding overlay badge styles...\n\nFor item 2179 I'll show \"68% OFF\" and for item 2509 \"15% OFF,\" keeping the quickview button positioning intact. I'm structuring the improvements array with What/Why entries and short descriptive identifiers instead of real hashes, then drafting the full HTML section by section before finalizing the JSON output.\n\nI'm deciding to leave the CTA button text mostly as-is, maybe adding a small shipping note beneath \"Add To Cart\" rather than altering the arrow styling, and skipping the mobile sticky footer promo idea. Now I'm ready to write out the final answer.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":""}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":20420,"completion_tokens":37026,"total_tokens":57446,"cost":1.02775,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":1.02775,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.1021,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.92565},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":4141,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}
