f (e.name.toString() == 'ReferenceError' ){\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\thasAdvancedOptions=false;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\tif(hasAdvancedOptions){\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tid=target.data().relHookdataId;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcontent_type=\\\"product_group\\\"\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\telse{\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tid=sku;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcontent_type=\\\"product\\\"\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\tif(pos==0){\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tids=\\\"'\\\"+id+\\\"'\\\";\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcurrency = target.data().relHookdataCurrency;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\telse{\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tids=ids+\\\",\\\"+\\\"'\\\"+id+\\\"'\\\";\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\tvar price = target.data().relHookdataPrice;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\ttotal+=parseFloat(price);\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\tpos = pos + 1;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n});\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\ntotal = total.toFixed(2);\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\nif(ids!=\\\"\\\"){\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\tids = \\\"[\\\"+ids+\\\"]\\\";\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\tfbq('track', 'ViewContent', {\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\tcontent_ids: ids,\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\tcontent_type: content_type,\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\tvalue: total,\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\tcurrency: currency\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t});\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n</script>\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n<noscript>\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n<img height='1' width='1' style='display:none' src='https://www.facebook.com/tr?id=731885793537364&ev=ViewContent&noscript=1' />\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n</noscript>\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t</body>\\n</html>\",\"improvements\":[{\"What\":\"Added a savings-focused hero area: benefit-driven subheadline under the H1, a trust/USP strip (in stock, easy returns, rewards, secure checkout, phone support) and a sale strip stating up to 68% off while stock lasts.\",\"Why\":\"Category pages with only 2 items convert on reassurance and urgency rather than choice. Trust signals reduce first-time-buyer anxiety and the savings/urgency framing gives a reason to buy now instead of bookmarking.\",\"Hash\":\"yd-usp-bar / yd-sale-strip\"},{\"What\":\"Upgraded product cards: replaced the generic 'Sale' badge with calculated 'Save 15%' / 'Save 68%' badges plus explicit dollar savings, added short benefit bullets, stock/clearance notes, and clearer CTAs ('Choose Color & Add to Cart', 'Add to Cart — $7.99').\",\"Why\":\"Quantified discounts are far more persuasive than the word 'Sale', and action-specific button copy sets expectations (options vs. direct add), which reduces click hesitation and cart abandonment.\",\"Hash\":\"yd-save / yd-you-save / buyitlink-text\"},{\"What\":\"Inserted a bulk/B2B block ('Teaching a kids' class or outfitting a studio?') linking to quantity pricing, custom printing, phone and quote request.\",\"Why\":\"Kids' mats are heavily bought by schools, camps and studios. Surfacing quantity discounts and custom printing captures high-AOV, repeat-order buyers who would otherwise buy one mat or leave.\",\"Hash\":\"yd-bulk\"},{\"What\":\"Added a cross-sell link block (kits & bundles, mat bags, blocks, straps, towels, kids' fitness, all mats, gift cards) and an intro copy section explaining why kids need their own mat.\",\"Why\":\"Increases average order value and gives visitors a next step when neither of the two mats fits, keeping them on site instead of bouncing to a competitor. The copy also adds keyword-rich content for organic traffic.\",\"Hash\":\"yd-crosssell / yd-cat-intro\"},{\"What\":\"Added an FAQ accordion (sizing, cleaning, bulk discounts, shipping/returns, rewards) with FAQPage structured data, plus ItemList/Product structured data for both mats and an improved SEO title/meta description.\",\"Why\":\"Pre-empts the objections that stall purchases and links to policy pages, while rich results (FAQ + product price/availability) improve SERP click-through and qualified traffic.\",\"Hash\":\"yd-faq / application-ld+json\"},{\"What\":\"Added a 'Not sure which mat to pick?' help block with phone and contact links, plus an 'Earn Rewards' top-nav link and a Quantity Discounts footer link.\",\"Why\":\"Assisted-sale prompts recover undecided shoppers (especially parents and teachers), and loyalty/quantity links drive repeat purchase and larger baskets.\",\"Hash\":\"yd-help\"},{\"What\":\"Fixed the broken Criteo listing-tag JavaScript (unescaped apostrophe in \\\"Kid's Yoga Mats\\\" caused a syntax error) and added add_to_cart event tracking to gtag and fbq on category card clicks.\",\"Why\":\"A JS syntax error silently killed the Criteo viewList tag, breaking retargeting on this page; capturing add-to-cart events improves ad bidding/audience quality and measurement of the funnel.\",\"Hash\":\"crto_category / add_to_cart event\"}]}","refusal":null,"reasoning":"I'm looking at this category page for kid's yoga mats with just two products and thinking through conversion improvements—trust badges, free shipping messaging, SEO copy, sale urgency with savings percentages, better product cards with review counts, and cross-sell suggestions to round out the page.\n\nI should also add email capture with a discount incentive, an FAQ section with schema markup, a sizing/buying guide for kids' mats, \"why shop with us\" trust points, stronger CTA copy, and a bulk/quantity discount callout aimed at schools and studios since teachers buying class sets could be a meaningful revenue driver. I'll also add subcategory links and product schema markup.\n\nI'm weighing whether to fetch the live URL to check existing CSS classes and styling, but since the HTML is already provided, I'll just do a quick fetch for confirmation and then write the improved HTML with inline styles for the new elements.\n\nFor the top banner, I want something compelling but factually grounded — savings percentages calculated from real prices, like the 68% discount on the $24.99 to $7.99 kids' mat, avoiding invented details like free shipping thresholds since I'm not certain those numbers are accurate.\n\nI'm planning several concrete additions: a category intro with SEO copy, savings badges on product cards using real computed discounts, a bulk/class-set banner targeting teachers linking to a quantity-discount page, a \"Complete the Practice\" cross-sell grid for related gear, and a trust bar highlighting rewards and secure checkout — while being careful not to fabricate stock or shipping claims.\n\nRather than risking a fabricated newsletter signup, I'll point users toward the real rewards registration page instead, and I'm also considering an FAQ accordion with schema markup, a clearer product count heading near sort options, and a kids' mat size guide table — while deliberately skipping any review ratings since I have no real data to back them up.\n\nNow I'm keeping sizing claims generic and hedged, echoing the safe \"sized just right for children through pre-teens\" language from the meta description, and planning to add secondary quick-view CTA buttons alongside a trust strip and style block right before the closing head tag.\n\nWriting trust strip HTML...\n\nFor the trust strip content, I'm sticking to verifiable claims: real customer service number, existing returns and rewards pages, secure checkout messaging, and a safe \"while supplies last\" urgency note rather than unverified shipping claims. I'm also considering small product card tweaks like a savings badge, though I want to be careful about changing CTA button text since it affects the add-to-cart flow.\n\nI'll adjust the CTA copy to \"Choose Options & Add\" and \"Add to Cart — $7.99\" instead of introducing fake countdown timers. For the FAQ section, I'm drafting genuine questions around sizing, non-slip material, cleaning instructions, and bulk discounts for schools, with answers linking back to real policy pages, plus building out structured data for FAQPage and Product schemas including offers and pricing for both items.\n\nI'll link out to related kids' gear categories, prefix all custom CSS classes with \"yd-\" to avoid conflicts, and skip a real newsletter form in favor of a simple CTA pointing to the rewards program page. For the heading, I'm going with \"Kids' Yoga Mats\" as the H1 with an SEO-friendly subhead, then assembling the full HTML output carefully escaping quotes within the JSON-LD blocks.\n\nI also spot a genuine bug in the original tracking script — a broken quote mismatch in the crto_category assignment — so I'm fixing it to use double quotes properly to prevent a JS parse error from breaking that script block. I'll keep the HTML readable with escaped newlines rather than jamming everything onto one literal line, since that formatting rule applies to the outer JSON structure, not the HTML content itself.\n\nNow I'm drafting the CSS for the trust-badge bar, category intro text block, and promo styling elements.\n\nWriting the bulk banner markup...\n\nI need to avoid fabricating a specific discount percentage, so I'll swap in safer wording like \"Save more when you buy more with quantity pricing.\" I also want a cross-sell grid using plain text links instead of images to dodge broken-image issues, plus a \"Back to all mats\" link, then move on to finalizing the product card HTML edits starting with pricing.\n\nI'm calculating the real discounts from the data: one mat drops from $19.99 to $16.99 (save $3, 15%), and the other from $24.99 to $7.99 (save $17, 68%). I'll label the bigger discount factually as \"68% Off — Lowest Price\" rather than inventing a \"Best Seller\" badge, skip fabricated return-policy details in favor of a plain \"Easy returns\" link to /returns, and keep the heading simple as \"2 Kids' Mats\" since a native `<details>` element handles the FAQ without extra JS complexity.\n\nI'm also refining the meta title for SEO/CTR, updating each product card's sale badge to show the real \"Save 15%\" / \"Save 68%\" text instead of generic \"Sale\", and adding JSON-LD structured data for the products while making sure existing email-protection links stay intact as I write out the full document with descriptive improvement identifiers.","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm looking at this category page for kid's yoga mats with just two products and thinking through conversion improvements—trust badges, free shipping messaging, SEO copy, sale urgency with savings percentages, better product cards with review counts, and cross-sell suggestions to round out the page.\n\nI should also add email capture with a discount incentive, an FAQ section with schema markup, a sizing/buying guide for kids' mats, \"why shop with us\" trust points, stronger CTA copy, and a bulk/quantity discount callout aimed at schools and studios since teachers buying class sets could be a meaningful revenue driver. I'll also add subcategory links and product schema markup.\n\nI'm weighing whether to fetch the live URL to check existing CSS classes and styling, but since the HTML is already provided, I'll just do a quick fetch for confirmation and then write the improved HTML with inline styles for the new elements.\n\nFor the top banner, I want something compelling but factually grounded — savings percentages calculated from real prices, like the 68% discount on the $24.99 to $7.99 kids' mat, avoiding invented details like free shipping thresholds since I'm not certain those numbers are accurate.\n\nI'm planning several concrete additions: a category intro with SEO copy, savings badges on product cards using real computed discounts, a bulk/class-set banner targeting teachers linking to a quantity-discount page, a \"Complete the Practice\" cross-sell grid for related gear, and a trust bar highlighting rewards and secure checkout — while being careful not to fabricate stock or shipping claims.\n\nRather than risking a fabricated newsletter signup, I'll point users toward the real rewards registration page instead, and I'm also considering an FAQ accordion with schema markup, a clearer product count heading near sort options, and a kids' mat size guide table — while deliberately skipping any review ratings since I have no real data to back them up.\n\nNow I'm keeping sizing claims generic and hedged, echoing the safe \"sized just right for children through pre-teens\" language from the meta description, and planning to add secondary quick-view CTA buttons alongside a trust strip and style block right before the closing head tag.\n\nWriting trust strip HTML...\n\nFor the trust strip content, I'm sticking to verifiable claims: real customer service number, existing returns and rewards pages, secure checkout messaging, and a safe \"while supplies last\" urgency note rather than unverified shipping claims. I'm also considering small product card tweaks like a savings badge, though I want to be careful about changing CTA button text since it affects the add-to-cart flow.\n\nI'll adjust the CTA copy to \"Choose Options & Add\" and \"Add to Cart — $7.99\" instead of introducing fake countdown timers. For the FAQ section, I'm drafting genuine questions around sizing, non-slip material, cleaning instructions, and bulk discounts for schools, with answers linking back to real policy pages, plus building out structured data for FAQPage and Product schemas including offers and pricing for both items.\n\nI'll link out to related kids' gear categories, prefix all custom CSS classes with \"yd-\" to avoid conflicts, and skip a real newsletter form in favor of a simple CTA pointing to the rewards program page. For the heading, I'm going with \"Kids' Yoga Mats\" as the H1 with an SEO-friendly subhead, then assembling the full HTML output carefully escaping quotes within the JSON-LD blocks.\n\nI also spot a genuine bug in the original tracking script — a broken quote mismatch in the crto_category assignment — so I'm fixing it to use double quotes properly to prevent a JS parse error from breaking that script block. I'll keep the HTML readable with escaped newlines rather than jamming everything onto one literal line, since that formatting rule applies to the outer JSON structure, not the HTML content itself.\n\nNow I'm drafting the CSS for the trust-badge bar, category intro text block, and promo styling elements.\n\nWriting the bulk banner markup...\n\nI need to avoid fabricating a specific discount percentage, so I'll swap in safer wording like \"Save more when you buy more with quantity pricing.\" I also want a cross-sell grid using plain text links instead of images to dodge broken-image issues, plus a \"Back to all mats\" link, then move on to finalizing the product card HTML edits starting with pricing.\n\nI'm calculating the real discounts from the data: one mat drops from $19.99 to $16.99 (save $3, 15%), and the other from $24.99 to $7.99 (save $17, 68%). I'll label the bigger discount factually as \"68% Off — Lowest Price\" rather than inventing a \"Best Seller\" badge, skip fabricated return-policy details in favor of a plain \"Easy returns\" link to /returns, and keep the heading simple as \"2 Kids' Mats\" since a native `<details>` element handles the FAQ without extra JS complexity.\n\nI'm also refining the meta title for SEO/CTR, updating each product card's sale badge to show the real \"Save 15%\" / \"Save 68%\" text instead of generic \"Sale\", and adding JSON-LD structured data for the products while making sure existing email-protection links stay intact as I write out the full document with descriptive improvement identifiers.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":""}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":18686,"completion_tokens":35191,"total_tokens":53877,"cost":0.973205,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.973205,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.09343,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.879775},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":3765,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}
