\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\telse{\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tid=sku;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcontent_type=\\\"product\\\"\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\tif(pos==0){\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tids=\\\"'\\\"+id+\\\"'\\\";\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tcurrency = target.data().relHookdataCurrency;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\telse{\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tids=ids+\\\",\\\"+\\\"'\\\"+id+\\\"'\\\";\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\tvar price = target.data().relHookdataPrice;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\ttotal+=parseFloat(price);\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t\\tpos = pos + 1;\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n});\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\ntotal = total.toFixed(2);\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\nif(ids!=\\\"\\\"){\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\tids = \\\"[\\\"+ids+\\\"]\\\";\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\tfbq('track', 'ViewContent', {\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\tcontent_ids: ids,\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\tcontent_type: content_type,\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\tvalue: total,\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t\\tcurrency: currency\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n\\t});\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n}\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n</script>\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n<noscript>\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n<img height='1' width='1' style='display:none' src='https://www.facebook.com/tr?id=731885793537364&ev=ViewContent&noscript=1' />\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\n</noscript>\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t</body>\\n</html>\",\"improvements\":[{\"What\":\"Rewrote the page title/meta description and H1 (\\\"Yoga Blankets\\\") with benefit + trust language (Mexican yoga blankets, free shipping $99+, studio pricing).\",\"Why\":\"Higher SERP click-through and immediate keyword/intent match on landing, which lifts qualified traffic and conversion.\",\"Hash\":\"seo-title-h1\"},{\"What\":\"Upgraded the top promo bar to lead with \\\"FREE Shipping on orders $99+\\\" plus links to Sale and studio/bulk pricing.\",\"Why\":\"Shipping cost is the #1 cart abandonment driver; stating the free-shipping threshold up front raises AOV and conversion.\",\"Hash\":\"promo-bar-freeship\"},{\"What\":\"Added a benefit-led category intro paragraph with an anchor link to a buying guide, plus a 4-item USP strip (free shipping, easy returns, studio/bulk pricing, rewards).\",\"Why\":\"Category pages that answer \\\"why buy here\\\" and \\\"which one\\\" reduce bounce and move undecided shoppers to product pages.\",\"Hash\":\"intro-usp-strip\"},{\"What\":\"Reordered the product grid so the best-value and 5-star top-rated blankets appear first and the out-of-stock item is moved last.\",\"Why\":\"Leading with the strongest social proof and price anchor increases click-through; burying sold-out stock prevents dead-end clicks.\",\"Hash\":\"grid-reorder\"},{\"What\":\"Added merchandising badges (Best Value, Top Rated ★5.0, Extra Heavy, New, Recycled, Back Soon) and one-line benefit blurbs to each product card, plus \\\"In stock · ready to ship\\\" microcopy.\",\"Why\":\"Scannable differentiators and stock reassurance help shoppers self-select quickly, raising product-page click-through and add-to-cart rate.\",\"Hash\":\"card-badges-blurbs\"},{\"What\":\"Changed the vague CTA \\\"Select Options\\\" to \\\"Choose Options →\\\" and converted the out-of-stock item's CTA to \\\"View Details\\\" with in-stock alternatives linked.\",\"Why\":\"Clear, action-oriented CTAs improve click rate, and redirecting sold-out demand to available items recovers otherwise lost revenue.\",\"Hash\":\"cta-clarity-oos\"},{\"What\":\"Made the sort dropdown auto-submit on change and marked the Blankets nav item active.\",\"Why\":\"Removes a hidden interaction step (many users never find the submit) and improves orientation, reducing friction and drop-off.\",\"Hash\":\"sort-autosubmit\"},{\"What\":\"Added a social-proof line under the product count (star rating + verified review mention) instead of the raw \\\"Products [6]\\\" label.\",\"Why\":\"Review-based social proof at the top of the grid is one of the strongest levers on category-page conversion.\",\"Hash\":\"social-proof-header\"},{\"What\":\"Inserted a \\\"Outfitting a studio or class?\\\" quantity-pricing block with CTA and phone number.\",\"Why\":\"Targets high-AOV studio buyers with the existing volume-discount program, increasing average order value and bulk orders.\",\"Hash\":\"bulk-studio-block\"},{\"What\":\"Added a \\\"Which yoga blanket is right for you?\\\" guide section linking each use case to a specific product.\",\"Why\":\"Guided selling resolves choice paralysis in a near-identical product set and adds internal links + SEO content.\",\"Hash\":\"buying-guide\"},{\"What\":\"Added a \\\"Complete your practice\\\" cross-sell row (bolsters, blocks, straps, kits) with a nudge about reaching the $99 free-shipping threshold.\",\"Why\":\"Drives multi-item baskets and pushes order totals over the free-shipping line, raising AOV.\",\"Hash\":\"cross-sell-row\"},{\"What\":\"Added an expandable FAQ section (use, washing, sizing, restorative choice, studio discounts, shipping/returns) with FAQPage and ItemList structured data.\",\"Why\":\"Answers pre-purchase objections without leaving the page and can win rich results for extra organic traffic.\",\"Hash\":\"faq-schema\"},{\"What\":\"Added a rewards-program callout and a \\\"Questions before you buy?\\\" support line with phone, email and live-chat mention; added help/secure-checkout reassurance in the footer.\",\"Why\":\"Loyalty incentive encourages purchase now, and visible human support plus trust signals reduce hesitation at the decision point.\",\"Hash\":\"rewards-support-trust\"}]}","refusal":null,"reasoning":"I could fetch the URL to get context on the existing page, but I think I can just improve the HTML directly without needing to fetch it first.I'm planning direct HTML improvements using CRO best practices: keeping the hero but adding a value proposition and trust bar, adding SEO-focused category copy, and enhancing product cards with rating placeholders, urgency badges, and clearer call-to-action labels like \"Choose Options →\" along with bestseller badges.\n\nFor the rest, I want to reorder out-of-stock items to the end with disabled \"Notify me\" buttons, make sort auto-submit on change, add a sticky mobile trust banner with free shipping progress, and include an FAQ section with schema markup for SEO. I'm also considering an email signup section, but I want to keep the offer generic rather than inventing a specific discount like \"10% off\" since I shouldn't fabricate promotions that may not be real.\n\nSince their code seems to reference a $99 free shipping threshold, I can reasonably use \"Free shipping on orders $99+\" as a supported claim. I'll add a bulk/studio orders banner pointing to quantity pricing, a cross-sell row linking to related categories like bolsters and blocks, and a \"Top Rated ★5.0 (6 reviews)\" badge on the item that actually has reviews, while avoiding unsupported claims like \"Studio Favorite.\" I'm also considering reordering products to put the reviewed, best-selling item earlier in the list.\n\nI'll skip unverifiable microcopy like shipping timeframes, but add \"In Stock — ready to ship\" labels and a note linking to volume pricing for studio buyers. For SEO, I'm planning to add ItemList structured data in JSON-LD for the products, and I'm wiring up the sort dropdown to auto-submit the form on change since the form already exists.\n\nNow I'm drafting the actual HTML: a style block for the new elements, an enhanced trust bar with free shipping promo text, a four-item USP row (free shipping, easy returns, volume pricing, rewards), and a short benefit-focused intro paragraph under the h1 linking to a buying guide.\n\nFor the product grid I'm adding enhancements, then a \"which blanket is right for you\" guidance section — since I don't have real specs, I'm keeping it soft and grounded in what I actually know: name, price, and review data, framing things like \"best value\" or \"top rated\" rather than inventing technical claims. After that I'm planning a cross-sell section for complementary yoga products.\n\nI'm also thinking through an FAQ accordion with generic, safe answers about care and sizing that point back to the product page rather than stating exact specs. For the email signup form, I'm unsure what endpoint to post to since I don't know the exact mailing-list integration, so I'm leaning toward a simple newsletter block rather than guessing at a risky form action.\n\nActually I decide instead to swap the newsletter form for a link to a rewards program page, since that's safer than a possibly broken POST endpoint and still drives conversions. I'm also adding a support strip with the phone number and chat option, making out-of-stock items link to \"View Details\" rather than add-to-cart, and planning the CSS along with an improved title/meta tag for SEO.\n\nNow I'm finalizing the meta description and moving into the actual HTML markup, adding badges like \"Best Value\" to product cards and keeping existing star ratings intact. For the call-to-action buttons on cards with color options, I'll go with \"Choose Options →\" as clearer and more accurate than a generic \"Select Options\" link, and I'm about to assemble the final JSON output with the improved HTML plus a list of the changes made.\n\nWriting CSS enhancements...\n\nAdding badge styles...\n\nAdding more CSS styles...\n\nI'm also planning sticky sort auto-submit behavior, aria labels for accessibility, and finalizing the product order with badges: Best Value, Top Rated, and marking the Extra Heavy Recycled blanket as out of stock with a \"Back Soon\" note at the end of the list.\n\nFor the out-of-stock card, I'm swapping the CTA to link directly to the product page instead of triggering an ajax add-to-cart action, and updating the heading to something like \"6 Yoga Blankets\" with a social proof line beneath it. I also want to add ItemList and FAQPage JSON-LD, making sure the FAQ schema content matches the visible FAQs exactly — covering blanket sizing and usage instructions like folding for seated poses and support under the hips.\n\nI'm working through the remaining FAQ answers: washability instructions (cold water, gentle cycle), which blankets suit restorative yoga best (heavier ones like Deluxe/Thunderbird), studio discount pricing with a link, and shipping/returns — phrasing free shipping over $99 softly and pointing to the Shipping Info page for full details.","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I could fetch the URL to get context on the existing page, but I think I can just improve the HTML directly without needing to fetch it first.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":""},{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm planning direct HTML improvements using CRO best practices: keeping the hero but adding a value proposition and trust bar, adding SEO-focused category copy, and enhancing product cards with rating placeholders, urgency badges, and clearer call-to-action labels like \"Choose Options →\" along with bestseller badges.\n\nFor the rest, I want to reorder out-of-stock items to the end with disabled \"Notify me\" buttons, make sort a